# Secrets & environment — NEVER commit real endpoints/keys (03-DEV-WORKFLOW §8)
vars.yaml
# Any per-cluster variant too. Only `vars.yaml` was ignored, so a second file for a second
# cluster (vars-cluster2.yaml, vars.staging.yaml, …) would have been TRACKED and carried a live
# MaaS key into git. Caught while wiring a second cluster, 2026-07-31.
vars*.yaml
**/vars*.yaml
# …but NOT the committed template. vars*.yaml matches vars.example.yaml too, which today survives only
# because it is already tracked (gitignore does not affect tracked files) — delete and recreate it and
# it would silently become unaddable. Negate it explicitly rather than rely on that.
!vars.example.yaml
!**/vars.example.yaml
*.kubeconfig
.env
.env.*
# Workshop bootstrap writes the generated user credentials here (never commit)
bootstrap/.credentials*

