www/
content/www/

# Local tooling noise
.DS_Store
*.log
.vale-cache/

# Claude Code local settings.
# The old note here claimed "project settings.json IS committed". That has been false since the
# 2026-07-19 owner review added the blanket `.claude/` below: the whole directory is ignored, so
# NOTHING under .claude/ is committed — settings.json and .claude/agents/ included, and
# `git ls-files .claude` returns zero. The two entries below are now redundant and are kept only
# as explicit intent: these two are per-machine regardless of how .claude/ is treated.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/launch.json

# kustomize helmCharts inflation pulls charts here at build time (Argo re-pulls on sync)
platform-portfolio/components/*/charts/

# Maintainer-local material (2026-07-19 owner review): present on maintainer machines,
# deliberately not part of the public tree.
.claude/
.vale/
.vale.ini
.yamllint.yaml
# docs/ was ignored WHOLESALE, which took docs/adr/ (architecture decision records) with it —
# they never reached the in-cluster Gitea mirror the attendee cockpits build from, and one of
# them (ADR-0002) went stale uncorrected because nobody could see it was even there (2026-07-31).
# Narrow the exclusion: docs/adr/ is public-repo content and stays tracked; everything else
# directly under docs/ (research notes, plans, reviews, module-template scratch, top-level
# maintainer notes) stays excluded exactly as before.
docs/*
!docs/adr/
# Contributor GUIDANCE is tracked too, for the same reason as the ADRs and with the same
# evidence: content/modules/ROOT/partials/*.adoc cite authoring-conventions.md AS AUTHORITY,
# and CLAUDE.md names it for the deprecated-tech ban list -- so a contributor cloning this
# repo got pages pointing at a file that was not there. Same defect shape as the stale ADR.
# Research notes, plans, reviews and triage scratch under docs/ stay excluded; media-capture-
# triage.md says 'Local-only' in its own header and is deliberately NOT listed here.
!docs/authoring-conventions.md
!docs/media-capture-conventions.md
AGENTS.md

# Office lock/temp files (created when a deck is open in PowerPoint)
~$*
tools/slides/
CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode (tools/media harness)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Python virtualenvs (tools/media/README.md tells you to create tools/media/.venv)
.venv/
venv/

# Capture-harness browser profile — A LIVE CREDENTIAL, and the reason this entry exists.
# tools/media/login.py persists an authenticated OpenShift console session into this directory:
# ~45 MB including Default/Cookies, a real session token for whoever logged in. It was NOT ignored
# until 2026-07-29, so a single `git add -A` would have committed a working console session to a
# public repo. The privacy guard cannot save you here — it runs `git grep`, which reads TEXT, and a
# cookie lives in a binary SQLite file it will never match. Delete the directory and re-run login.py
# rather than ever committing it.
# GLOBS, not the two literal names that used to be here. OGSR_PROFILE lets you point login.py at ANY
# profile directory, and running several attendee identities in parallel means names like
# shot-profile-user3 / shot-profile-user6. Those were untracked-but-NOT-ignored (checked 2026-07-31),
# so the very workflow the harness is built for would have walked a live session token past this
# entry. Note the session file is JSON — plain text, unlike the cookie DB above — so it is the one
# the privacy guard MIGHT catch, but only if the cluster domain inside it happens to match a pattern
# the guard knows; do not rely on that.
tools/media/shot-profile*/
tools/media/shot-profile*.session.json

# Capture scratch. Media lanes iterate on a shot — debug frames, half-loaded pages, wrong-state
# captures — and some of that lands in content/modules/ROOT/assets/, which is a PUBLISHED directory:
# anything committed there ships to attendees. Underscore-prefix is the scratch convention; nothing
# tracked uses it (checked 2026-07-31 before adding this). A real capture earns a real name.
# This matters more than tidiness: a debug frame is whatever the page happened to show when the
# capture failed, which can include a login form or an error page nobody reviewed.
content/modules/ROOT/assets/**/_*
tools/media/_*
